WEBVTT

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.520
Wow, just look at that.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.020
How magnificent.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:56.410
Entering through the village's main gate are carriages loaded with dowry.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:04.390
Secret Within the Mist

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.500
Onee-chan!

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.410
She's so beautiful!

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.390
Yeah.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.760
Welcome back, Saju.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.640
Welcome, Erin-chan.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.850
Hello.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.420
The square was filled with cattle and sheep.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.840
Everyone was so surprised.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.890
The dowry must be here.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.350
The groom is the son of the Saka Village chief.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:47.020
Essentially, you've been promised a life without any inconveniences.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.070
I want things to stay the way they are.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:56.860
You never ask for too much, do you?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.910
I want to learn more of your recipes.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.200
You don't need to know my country cooking.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.670
You will have better things to eat over there.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:12.190
And you even have such a beautiful wedding dress.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.160
I want to wear something like this, too.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.060
You'll get to when your time to be married arrives.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.140
Really?

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.910
Yes.  Just like Soju.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.250
When that time comes, your father will prepare one for you.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.360
I can't wait for it.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:36.290
Grandma!

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.820
I brought some congratulatory rice cakes from the assembly hall.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.600
They smell so nice.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.720
Really!

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.770
They smell like flowers.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:49.830
Saju!

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:50.900
You can't!

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:55.830
Congratulatory rice cakes are to usher in luck, so only the bride can have them.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.330
Be a good girl about it, okay?

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.300
Sure.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.100
Soju, you haven't eaten anything all day, have you?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.600
Here, have some.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:07.990
Yeah.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.850
Mom, where's Dad?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.750
He's at the ponds.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.210
Did he say anything?

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.530
Let's see...  He was the same as usual.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.560
I see.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.420
Isn't today a day off?

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:55.820
Yeah, but right now I have to work hard for Soju.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.000
For Soju?

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.260
Once she leaves this place, I won't be able to do anything for her.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.760
So right now, I have to work hard for her.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:16.360
All right, let's hem up the dress, shall we?

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:18.860
Yeah.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.170
Onee-chan!

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:31.370
Soju!

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.570
Soju!  Wake up!

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:34.020
Onee-chan!

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:34.830
Soju!

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.520
I'm going to go get my mom!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:36.900
Onee-chan, wake up!

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.200
What happened?!
Onee-chan, wake up!

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.200
What's wrong with you, Soju?!

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.350
Onee-chan...

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:02.650
Judging from the symptoms, she might be under the effect of some sort of poison.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.030
"Poison?"

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.490
I can smell the scent of flowers coming from her sweat.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.630
"Flowers?"

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:17.980
Mom!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.980
This is the rice cake that Soju-chan ate.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.040
This rice cake has a flowery scent.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.140
Where did this come from?

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.380
The village assembly hall.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.630
Erin, run and bring them here!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:36.400
Okay.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:49.920
Some chichi mimic is mixed in with the leaves.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:53.280
Chichi mimic is a lethal poison.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.520
Mom!

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.960
It looks similar to the leaves put in the congratulatory rice cakes, so they must have mistaken it.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.660
Soju!

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.620
Soju!

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.220
Soju...

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.520
Dear...

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.260
What about Soyon?!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.210
Have you had Soyon look at her?!

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:25.780
Yes.  She's over at the Chief's place to negotiate the purchase of some antidote.

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.300
Soju...

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.670
What are we going to do?!

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:40.080
We already accepted the dowry!

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.830
If we let Soju die...

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.250
Calm down, Wadan!

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.030
How is Soju looking?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.320
If we leave her be, the poison will have circulated throughout her entire body by the third day,

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.280
and she will die by the seventh.

00:07:53.810 --> 00:08:00.020
If such a thing happens, Ake Village will lose the other villages' trust.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.250
Wadan, Soju's life takes priority here.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.900
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.220
But still, chichi mimic of all things...

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.380
Oji-san.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.800
Chief, please save Soju.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.150
I beg of you!

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:30.650
It's something I bought for Soju from a merchant.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.320
A hairpin?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.350
Something so expensive...

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.790
Please, save her with this.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:41.400
Either way, to ask help from a doctor at the capital or to ask my own connections,

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:44.820
would result in taking days to obtain an antidote.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.470
The question is whether Soju will last until then.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:48.870
I have a request to make.

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:52.970
Will you permit me to go to the Mist Point?

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.720
"The Mist Point?!"

00:08:56.040 --> 00:09:00.140
If it's to the Mist Point, I can obtain the antidote in under a week.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:06.650
I decided never to associate with the Mist People.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:12.720
But to meet the deadline of the wedding day, we have no choice but to go to the Mist Point.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.060
Chief!

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:30.030
That hairpin alone won't be enough to pay for the medicine.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:32.130
Use the village's funds.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.950
Thank you very much!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.640
Soyon.  You must cure Soju before the wedding without fail.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:39.910
Do you understand?

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:41.860
Yes.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.110
Mom, I want to go with you.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:54.270
I want to save Soju-chan.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.890
We're not going there for fun.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.190
I want to become a doctor like you.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.330
I want to learn many things.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.610
Not just about Touda.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:11.130
I want to become a doctor that could save Soju-chan, too.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.490
Please!

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.980
I wonder where I stashed your raincoat.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:28.860
We'll be trekking through the mountains, so hurry and get prepared.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:32.940
Okay!

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:06.300
Mom, when you were married, did you travel this path?

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:11.410
That's right.  I came from the forest covered in mist, beyond this path.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:15.350
It was also in that forest that I met your father.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.550
Really?

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:23.160
Your father was on a deer hunt, but slipped off the cliff.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:28.620
He had hit his head hard, and his leg was broken, too.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.380
So you saved him, right?

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:36.680
He was a very kind man.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:42.250
He was worried about you, who was still unborn, and I until the very end,

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:47.940
and asked your grandfather to allow us to stay in Ake Village even after he was gone.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:54.380
I was an Overseer for the Mist Points.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:12:01.530
A Mist Point is where trade occurs between
the Mist People and others.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.130
Really?

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:09.030
Only Overseers and Explorers are allowed to travel away from the clan.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.830
What do the other people do?

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.580
"Never remain in one place."

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.520
"Never marry anyone outside of the clan."

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:21.870
They live, abiding by their old code.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.090
Is this really the place?

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:36.780
That's right.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.010
This will do.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.780
What?  Just this?!

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:49.620
The name of the medicine we want is written on that paper, right?

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.720
When the mist envelops this area, an Overseer will exchange those for what we want.

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:58.120
Soju is at a crucial point from here on.

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:01.070
I might not be able to leave her side.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:04.990
If that happens, you'll come to pick up the medicine, okay?

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:07.470
Okay.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:17.130
Ever since going to the Mist Point,

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.570
even while cooking,

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.130
or even while making polish balls,

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:27.250
she was anxious to see whether the mist was enveloping Cone Mountain.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.050
Hey, Erin.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.210
The hairpin is gone!

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:41.940
The Overseer must have come!

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:54.360
It's cold.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:59.050
Please.  Come fast.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:01.380
Hurry and bring Soju-chan's medicine.

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.230
Are you the Overseer?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.450
Wait!

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:48.980
Please don't go!

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.570
Without the medicine, Soju-chan is going to die!

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:07.100
Please!  Give us the medicine!

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:08.280
Please!

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:11.530
Please!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.270
These are...

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.880
Thank you very much!

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:02.270
Mom!  Mom!

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:03.830
Erin!

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:05.380
I brought the medicine.

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:06.840
Really?!

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:09.860
A man of the Mist People brought it.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.090
Hurry and give it to Soju-chan.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:17.560
Thank you, Erin-chan!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.840
Soju, Erin-chan brought the medicine for you.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:41.690
Saju.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.600
Erin-chan.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.430
They stayed up all night, so they haven't had much sleep.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.640
So let them sleep.

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:53.220
Looks like your fever has gone down.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:57.740
I think you're fine now, but drink this up.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.500
Soyon-san...

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:09.900
Are you happy to have married into this village?

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:18.080
I'm sorry.  You're the only person I know who has married into this village.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:25.760
That medicine is made by the Mist People, the place where I came from.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:31.000
Erin brought it from Cone Mountain.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:37.280
The first time I met Asson was at Sammok's Cliff.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:40.100
At such a misty place?

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:41.220
Yes.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:46.230
I found Asson lying on the ground while I was looking for medicinal herbs growing along the cliff.

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:57.620
He went alone on a deer hunt, despite the danger, in order to cure his sickly father.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:05.180
A deer's liver is very nutritious, so he wanted to have him eat it.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.170
That sounds a little like Erin-chan.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:11.190
You're right.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:18.230
I'm happy enough to have her next to me.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:22.600
My father might not be thinking the same as you.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:29.500
If I get married, I may never be able to come back to this village,

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.880
yet he's working until very late every day.

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:37.960
He doesn't care about me.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:46.940
Father.

00:19:48.010 --> 00:19:56.150
Your father was working late in order to buy you an expensive hairpin.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:03.370
But that hairpin has now gone to buy the antidote.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:16.780
It might not suit your tastes, but this is a hairpin I made using Touda scales.

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.230
Father...

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:50.250
Thank you...

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.120
Hey, don't push.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:09.290
Here she comes.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:27.400
Hey.  That hairpin is made from a Touda's second-layer scales.

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:34.250
Thank you for your years of care.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.490
Have a happy life.

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:38.460
Take care of yourself.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:40.920
Congratulations, Soju!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:41.920
Take care!

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:43.510
Seize your happiness!

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:44.410
Congratulations!

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:49.640
Thank you!  Thank you!

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:51.920
Onee-chan!

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:53.580
Take care!

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:09.970
I wonder if a day like this will come for Erin, too.

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.590
I won't go anywhere.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.500
I'll always be with you, Mom.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:08.360
Soon, it will be the Touda Egg-Hunting Day that happens once a year at the swamp.

00:24:08.830 --> 00:24:13.720
I'm ten years old now, so Dad is
finally taking me with him!

00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:17.800
But what we found at the swamp instead were two strangers.

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:20.640
Could they be egg thieves?

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:24.990
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Erin and the Egg Thieves.

00:24:24.990 --> 00:24:25.010
Erin and the Egg Thieves
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Erin and the Egg Thieves.

00:24:25.010 --> 00:24:29.990
Erin and the Egg Thieves
